Aim

To create effective headlines for Google Ads campaigns.

Beginner Level Exact Steps
Step 1: Open Browser

Open Google Chrome.

Step 2: Open Google Ads

Go to:

Google Ads

Step 3: Login with Gmail
Enter Gmail ID
Enter password
Login successfully
Step 4: Open Search Ads Section
In dashboard click Campaigns
Click New Campaign
Select:
Website traffic OR Sales
Step 5: Select Search Campaign

Choose:

Search Campaign
Step 6: Understand Google Ad Headlines

Observe:

Headlines appear at top of Google search ads
Headlines attract customers
Headlines should be short and clear
Step 7: Choose Product or Service

Example:

Food delivery
Mobile shop
Online course
Restaurant

Example selected:

Online Food Delivery
Step 8: Write Attractive Headlines

Rules:

Use simple words
Add keywords
Mention offers
Use action words
Step 9: Create Sample Headlines
Example Headlines
Order Food Online Today
Fast Food Delivery Near You
Get 50% Discount Now
Fresh Food Delivered Fast
Best Online Food Service
Step 10: Check Character Limit

Google Ads headline limit:

Maximum 30 characters

Ensure headlines are short.

Step 11: Add Description

Example:

Order delicious food online with fast delivery and great discounts.
Step 12: Save Headlines in MS Word

Create document containing:

Aim
Procedure
Sample headlines
Description

Save as:

GoogleAdsHeadlines.docx
Step 13: Take Screenshots

Take screenshots of:

Google Ads dashboard
Search campaign page
Headlines created

